<p>Career breaks are not unique to tech, and as such, advice on how to pres=
ent these are not unique, either. The article <a href=3D"https://www.monste=
r.co.uk/career-advice/article/career-break-cv-example" target=3D"_blank" re=
l=3D"noopener noreferrer">How to explain the time off during your career br=
eak</a> on Monster UK gives some good suggestions on how to word specific s=
ituations:</p>
<p><em>You went traveling: =E2=80=9CI fulfilled my life-long dream of trave=
ling through South America for six months, where I improved my Spanish and =
gained an understanding of different cultures.=E2=80=9D</em></p>
<p><em>You wanted a fresh start: =E2=80=9CI chose to take time off work to =
pursue my interest in painting and had the time to decide on a new career p=
ath that really fits my personal goals.=E2=80=9D</em></p>
<p><em>You were ill: =E2=80=9CI took time off work due to a lengthy illness=
, but the time off allowed me to fully regain fitness for the long-term and=
 I became involved in volunteering at a local charity shop to get me back i=
nto the swing of work.=E2=80=9D</em></p>
<p><em>You were caring for someone else: =E2=80=9CI took time off to care f=
or my brother, who has now made a full recovery.=E2=80=9D</em></p>
<h2 id=3D"study-related-career-breaks">Study Related Career Breaks</h2>
<p>For a career break where you spent time learning new skills=E2=80=94tech=
nologies, languages=E2=80=94it=E2=80=99s a good idea to add this similar to=
 a work experience, with proof that you=E2=80=99ve mastered these skills. W=
ork that is in production always speaks more than completing a course, or d=
oing self-study. Aim to use the results and impact framework, to quantify w=
hy a project you completed was interesting or difficult.</p>
<p>Most people will create portfolio projects as an outcome of their studie=
s. While this is not bad, it=E2=80=99s both very common, and building a pro=
ject that=E2=80=99s used by only you is not a strong indication of what you=
 can do on the job. If you want to stand out, go beyond this. Prove that yo=
u mastered a technology by shipping something in production, teaching what =
you learned=E2=80=94writing articles, mentoring others=E2=80=94or contribut=
ing to open source projects using the same technology.</p>
